BORE on linux-cachyos 7.3.1: 7.3.1 added update_protect_slice(), which reads
normalized_sysctl_sched_base_slice; the BORE patch (cachyos/kernel-patches 7.3/sched/
0001-bore-cachy.patch, still written for 7.3-rc2 as of 2026-10-31) only declares that
variable without CONFIG_SCHED_BORE, so the build stops with "use of undeclared identifier".
Same substitution the patch itself makes in set_protect_slice() a few lines above.
kernel-update applies this after prepare() and skips it once it is already upstream.

--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -1172,7 +1172,11 @@
 static inline void update_protect_slice(struct cfs_rq *cfs_rq, struct sched_entity *se)
 {
 	u64 vruntime = min_vruntime(se->vruntime, avg_vruntime(cfs_rq));
+#ifdef CONFIG_SCHED_BORE
+	u64 slice = sysctl_sched_base_slice;
+#else /* CONFIG_SCHED_BORE */
 	u64 slice = normalized_sysctl_sched_base_slice;
+#endif /* CONFIG_SCHED_BORE */
 	u64 vprot;
 
 	if (sched_feat(RUN_TO_PARITY))
